#. type: Title =
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:1
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build Systems"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:7
msgid ""
"The build system is the primary way for both developers and system "
"integrators to interact with the Git project. As such, being easy to use and "
"extend for those who are not directly developing Git itself is just as "
"important as other requirements we have on any potential build system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:10
msgid ""
"This document outlines the different requirements that we have for the build "
"system and then compares available build systems using these criteria."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:11
#, no-wrap
msgid "Requirements"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:15
msgid ""
"The following subsections present a list of requirements that we have for "
"any potential build system. Sections are sorted by decreasing priority."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:16
#, no-wrap
msgid "Platform support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:20
msgid ""
"The build system must have support for all of our platforms that we "
"continually test against as outlined by our platform support policy. These "
"platforms are:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:22
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:183
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:212
msgid "Linux"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:23
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:186
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:216
msgid "Windows"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:24
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:187
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:217
msgid "macOS"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:27
msgid ""
"Furthermore, the build system should have support for the following "
"platforms that generally have somebody running test pipelines against "
"regularly:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:29
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:180
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:207
msgid "AIX"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:30
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:182
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:210
msgid "FreeBSD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:31
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:213
msgid "NetBSD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:32
msgid "NonStop"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:33
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:184
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:214
msgid "OpenBSD"
msgstr ""

