#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:40
#, no-wrap
msgid "Auto-detection of supported features"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:45
msgid ""
"The build system must support auto-detection of features which are or aren't "
"available on the current platform. Platform maintainers should not be "
"required to manually configure the complete build."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:47
msgid "Auto-detection of the following items is considered to be important:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:49
msgid "Check for the existence of headers."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:50
msgid "Check for the existence of libraries."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:51
msgid "Check for the existence of exectuables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:52
msgid "Check for the runtime behavior of specific functions."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:54
msgid ""
"Check for specific link order requirements when multiple libraries are "
"involved."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:55
#, no-wrap
msgid "Ease of use"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:60
msgid ""
"The build system should be both easy to use and easy to extend. While this "
"is naturally a subjective metric it is likely not controversial to say that "
"some build systems are considerably harder to use than others."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:61
#, no-wrap
msgid "IDE support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:64
msgid ""
"The build system should integrate with well-known IDEs. Well-known IDEs "
"include:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:66
msgid "Microsoft Visual Studio"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:67
msgid "Visual Studio Code"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:68
msgid "Xcode"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:70
msgid "There are four levels of support:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:72
msgid "Native integration into the IDE."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:73
msgid "Integration into the IDE via a plugin."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:75
msgid ""
"Integration into the IDE via generating a project description with the build "
"system."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:76
msgid "No integration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:80
msgid ""
"Native integration is preferable, but integration via either a plugin or by "
"generating a project description via the build system are considered "
"feasible alternatives."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:83
msgid ""
"Another important distinction is the level of integration. There are two "
"features that one generally wants to have:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:85
msgid "Integration of build targets."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:87
msgid ""
"Automatic setup of features like code completion with detected build "
"dependencies."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:90
msgid ""
"The first bullet point is the bare minimum, but is not sufficient to be "
"considered proper integration."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:91
#, no-wrap
msgid "Out-of-tree builds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:96
msgid ""
"The build system should support out-of-tree builds. Out-of-tree builds allow "
"a developer to configure multiple different build directories with different "
"configuration, e.g. one \"debug\" build and one \"release\" build."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:97
#, no-wrap
msgid "Cross-platform builds"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:101
msgid ""
"The build system should support cross-platform builds, e.g. building for arm "
"on an x86-64 host."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:102
#, no-wrap
msgid "Language support"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:106
msgid ""
"The following languages and toolchains are of relevance and should be "
"supported by the build system:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:109
msgid ""
"C: the primary compiled language used by Git, must be supported. Relevant "
"toolchains are GCC, Clang and MSVC."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:111
msgid ""
"Rust: candidate as a second compiled lanugage, should be supported. Relevant "
"toolchains is the LLVM-based rustc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:115
msgid ""
"Built-in support for the respective languages is preferred over support that "
"needs to be wired up manually to avoid unnecessary complexity. Native "
"support includes the following features:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:117
msgid "Compiling objects."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:118
msgid "Dependency tracking."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:119
msgid "Detection of available features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:120
msgid "Discovery of relevant toolchains."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:121
msgid "Linking libraries and executables."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:122
msgid "Templating placeholders in scripts."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:123
#, no-wrap
msgid "Test integration"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:128
msgid ""
"It should be possible to integrate tests into the build system such that it "
"is possible to build and test Git within the build system. Features which "
"are nice to have:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:131
msgid ""
"Track build-time dependencies for respective tests. Unit tests have "
"different requirements than integration tests."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:132
msgid "Allow filtering of which tests to run."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:133
msgid "Allow running tests such that utilities like `test_pause` or `debug` work."
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ==
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:134
#, no-wrap
msgid "Comparison"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:137
msgid "The following list of build systems are considered:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:139
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:143
#, no-wrap
msgid "GNU Make"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:140
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:158
#, no-wrap
msgid "autoconf"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:141
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:175
#, no-wrap
msgid "CMake"
msgstr ""

#. type: Title ===
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:142
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:202
#, no-wrap
msgid "Meson"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:146
msgid ""
"Platform support: ubitquitous on all platforms, but not well-integrated into "
"Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:147
msgid "Auto-detection: no built-in support for auto-detection of features."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:149
msgid ""
"Ease of use: easy to use, but discovering available options is "
"hard. Makefile rules can quickly get out of hand once reaching a certain "
"scope."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:150
msgid "IDE support: execution of Makefile targets is supported by many IDEs"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:151
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:168
msgid "Out-of-tree builds: supported in theory, not wired up in practice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:152
msgid "Cross-platform builds: supported in theory, not wired up in practice."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:153
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:170
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:196
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:224
msgid "Language support:"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:154
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:171
msgid "C: Limited built-in support, many parts need to be wired up manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:155
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:172
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:198
msgid "Rust: No built-in support, needs to be wired up manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:157
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:174
msgid ""
"Test integration: partially supported, many parts need to be wired up "
"manually."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:161
msgid ""
"Platform support: ubiquitous on all platforms, but not well-integrated into "
"Windows."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:162
msgid "Auto-detection: supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:165
msgid ""
"Ease of use: easy to use, discovering available options is comparatively "
"easy. The autoconf syntax is prohibitively hard to extend though due to its "
"complex set of interacting files and the hard-to-understand M4 language."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:167
msgid ""
"IDE support: no integration into IDEs at generation time. The generated "
"Makefiles have the same level of support as GNU Make."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:169
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:195
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:223
msgid "Cross-platform builds: supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:179
msgid ""
"Platform support: not as extensive as GNU Make or autoconf, but all major "
"platforms are supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:181
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:208
msgid "Cygwin"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:185
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:215
msgid "Solaris"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:190
msgid ""
"Ease of use: easy to use, discovering available options is not always "
"trivial. The scripting language used by CMake is somewhat cumbersome to use, "
"but extending CMake build instructions is doable."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:193
msgid ""
"IDE support: natively integrated into Microsoft Visual Studio. Can generate "
"project descriptions for Xcode. An extension is available for Visual Studio "
"Code. Many other IDEs have plugins for CMake."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:194
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:222
msgid "Out-of-tree builds: supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:197
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:225
msgid "C: Supported for GCC, Clang, MSVC and other toolchains."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:201
msgid ""
"Test integration: supported, even though test dependencies are a bit "
"cumbersome to use via \"test fixtures\". Interactive test runs are not "
"supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:206
msgid ""
"Platform: not as extensive as GNU Make or autoconf, but all major platforms "
"and some smaller ones are supported."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:209
msgid "DragonflyBSD"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:211
msgid "Haiku"
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:219
msgid ""
"Ease of use: easy to use, discovering available options is easy. The "
"scripting language is straight-forward to use."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:221
msgid ""
"IDE support: Supports generating build instructions for Xcode and Microsoft "
"Visual Studio, a plugin exists for Visual Studio Code."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:226
msgid "Rust: Supported for rustc."
msgstr ""

#. type: Plain text
#: ../Documentation-sedout/technical/build-systems.adoc:227
msgid ""
"Test integration: supported. Interactive tests are supported starting with "
"Meson 1.5.0 via the `--interactive` flag."
msgstr ""
